      "text": "303908.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **764** and **397**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 764 by 7 (the ones place digit of 397):**\n   \n   \\[\n   764 \\times 7 = 5348\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 764 by 90 (the tens place digit of 397):**\n   \n   \\[\n   764 \\times 90 = 68760\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 764 by 300 (the hundreds place digit of 397):**\n   \n   \\[\n   764 \\times 300 = 229200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   5348 + 68760 + 229200 = 303908\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{303908}\n\\]",
