      "text": "428 \u00d7 775 = 831700.\n\n# Answer\nThe product of 428 and 775 is \\boxed{831700}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 428 and 775, we can break down the multiplication into three steps based on the place values of the digits in 775.\n\n1. **Multiply 428 by the ones place digit (5) of 775:**\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 5 = 2140\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 428 by the tens place digit (70) of 775:**\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 70 = 29960\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 428 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 775:**\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 700 = 299600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   2140 + 29960 + 299600 = 831700\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 428 and 775 is \\boxed{831700}.",
